=== task: predict easy
title: Read and write
code:
```python
def remove_all(nums, unwanted):
    write = 0
    for read in range(len(nums)):
        if nums[read] != unwanted:
            nums[write] = nums[read]
            write += 1
    del nums[write:]
    return nums

print(remove_all([7, 7, 2, 7, 5], 7), remove_all([1, 2], 9))
```
wrong[[7, 7, 2, 7, 5] [1, 2]]: The function copies each kept item to the front and deletes the rest: the 7s are gone.
wrong[[2, 5, 2, 7, 5] [1, 2]]: After the loop, write is 2, and `del nums[2:]` deletes everything from index 2 on.
wrong[[2, 5] []]: Nothing in `[1, 2]` is 9, so every item is kept.
