=== task: fill medium
title: Until one list runs out
prompt: Fill in the blanks so that `merge` works, and the program prints:

```output
[1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 9]
```
code:
```python
def merge(a, b):
    i = 0
    j = 0
    out = []
    while i < len(a) ?? j < len(b):
        if a[i] <= b[j]:
            out.append(a[i])
            i += 1
        else:
            out.append(b[j])
            j += 1
    out.extend(a[??:])
    out.extend(b[j:])
    return out

print(merge([2, 8, 9], [1, 3, 5]))
```
